# Form calculator

This live `%form` example exercises a recursive form tree and callbacks from a
drop-down and slider. Choose a standard function and change its range; the
curve is drawn on the form's canvas by WCHNT code.

## Schema

```
Calculator = Form :Graph Inbox @WCHNTMaths/maths @WCHNTForm/ui
Form = Panel/root
Panel = String/id [Node]/children
Node = Panel | Label | TextInput | TextArea | Slider | Button | Options | Canvas
Label = String/id String/text
TextInput = String/id String/value
TextArea = String/id String/value Int/rows Int/cols
Slider = String/id Float/min Float/max Float/step Float/value
Button = String/id String/text
Option = String/value String/label
Options = String/id [Option]/options String/selected
Canvas = String/id Int/width Int/height
Graph = String/id Int/width Int/height
>Inbox = String/function Float/range
```

## Construction

```
[:Calculator
  [:Form
    [:Panel "calculator"
      [:Array/Node
        [:Label "formula-label" "Formula"]
        [:Options "function"
          [:Array/Option
            [:Option "sin" "sin(x)"]
            [:Option "cos" "cos(x)"]
            [:Option "tan" "tan(x)"]
            [:Option "sqrt" "sqrt(x)"]]
          "sin"]
        [:Slider "range" 1.0 20.0 0.1 10.0]
        [:Canvas "graph" 800 400]]]]
  [:Graph "graph" 800 400]
  [:Inbox "sin" 10.0]
  maths
  ui]
```

## Methods

```
Inbox::update! = { [:Inbox function range] }

Graph::valueAt = { Float/x |
  switch (theCalculator.inbox.function)
    "sin" -> { theCalculator.maths.sin(x) }
    "cos" -> { theCalculator.maths.cos(x) }
    "tan" -> { theCalculator.maths.tan(x) }
    else -> { theCalculator.maths.sqrt(x) }
}

Graph::draw = { @WCHNTGraphics/g |
  range = theCalculator.inbox.range.
  step = range / 160.0.
  xScale = width / range.
  yScale = height / 2.0.
  styled = g.clear().lineStyle(1, 0xffffffff).
  segments = 160.times({ Int/i |
    x1 = i * step.
    x2 = (i + 1) * step.
    y1 = this.valueAt(x1).
    y2 = this.valueAt(x2).
    g.drawLine(x1 * xScale, yScale - (y1 * yScale / 2.0),
               x2 * xScale, yScale - (y2 * yScale / 2.0))
  }).
  g
}

Calculator::step = {
  nextFunction = ui.value("function").
  nextRange = ui.number("range").
  nextInput = [:Inbox nextFunction nextRange].
  next = [:Calculator form graph nextInput maths ui].
  drawn = next.graph.draw(ui.graphics("graph")).
  next
}
```

## Target

```
%form

%requires
WCHNTMaths
WCHNTMaths::sin(Float) -> Float
WCHNTMaths::cos(Float) -> Float
WCHNTMaths::tan(Float) -> Float
WCHNTMaths::sqrt(Float) -> Float
WCHNTForm
WCHNTForm::value(String) -> String
WCHNTForm::number(String) -> Float
WCHNTForm::graphics(String) -> WCHNTGraphics
WCHNTGraphics
WCHNTGraphics::clear() -> WCHNTGraphics
WCHNTGraphics::lineStyle(Int,Int) -> WCHNTGraphics
WCHNTGraphics::drawLine(Float,Float,Float,Float) -> WCHNTGraphics

%init
function init() {
    calculator = CalculatorAssemblage.factory(wchntMaths, wchntForm);
    wchntForm.mount(calculator.form);
    calculator.graph.draw(wchntForm.graphics("graph"));
}

%step
function step() {
    calculator = calculator.step();
}
```
